soma run --fresh app.cell ; soma run app.cell A.go p ; soma run app.cell Worker.show r → lit ; soma run app.cell Worker.show p → off. The same handler A.go emits flip: started by runtime { } its interior hears it, started as `soma run app.cell A.go` it does not (plain interpreter, interior not registered). STRUCTURE_DESIGN §4 says every path answers the same way, except serve and test; `soma run app.cell P.h` is a third exception, unsaid (commands/run.rs: only the runtime section and Child.h use runtime::Runtime). The analyses assume it heard (over-approximation: no false ✓, but the rule is not one).
Same cause, second entry path: app2.cell — soma run --fresh app2.cell prints nothing: Desk's runtime calls Hub.go, Hub (top-level) emits flip, and Hub's own interior Worker never hears it — Runtime::scope_interpreter registers the interior of the MAIN cell only (runtime/mod.rs:195-201). check and the product search assume the rule (Worker hears).
